{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanReply":true,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":22,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":true,"HasAttachments":true,"Views":2050,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":1899554,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1439827749","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":132,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"StartDate":1435675350,"LastPoster":{"Id":284800,"Name":"Svitlana","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":false},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":60,"Preview":{"Id":1899554,"PostDate":1435675350,"PostContent":"We are just coming down from our post wedding high! \u00a0There is nothing quite like it. \u00a0 \u00a0 I have b...","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Married on June 20th, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess Riviera Gazebo & Reception at the Chill Out with 60 guests<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>My review thread: \u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79344-grand-sunset-princess-platinum-yucatan-princess-wedding\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79344-grand-sunset-princess-platinum-yucatan-princess-wedding\/<\/a>","Email":"rebecca.valero@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1396968452,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1439827749","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":132,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"veryvalentine","Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"<strong>Edited by veryvalentine, 30 June 2015 - 02:54 PM.<\/strong>","EditDate":1435676058,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":8,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"31a353f8aae5ac9465e418ff098dd03d","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;We are just coming down from our post wedding high! &amp;nbsp;There is nothing quite like it. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I have been writing our wedding review but I wanted to write this post first to seek some advice from other past brides.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Everything went well, there were some small glitches that I will write more about on our review, but essentially the experience was the best time of my life. &amp;nbsp;It was a combination of the people who went, the beauty of the beach and resort that contributed to a perfect day. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;When we left the resort I started crying because I knew that I had just spent the best time of my life at this resort with a group of people that I may never have all together again. &amp;nbsp;Our guests traveled from England, Peru, Spain, parts of Mexico,Toronto and Windsor so it&#039;s probably safe to say that they won&#039;t all be in the same room again. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I have never felt an overwhelming feeling of happiness and gratitude as this before and the advice I took with me from previous brides was to stop and really take it in. &amp;nbsp;There was a point where I was doing the bouquet toss and my dad&#039;s wife introduce a Mexican tradition which is to do a serpent dance (follow the leader type of dance) and all the women were wearing veils that she had made and they were dancing around me...everyone was so in the moment and so happy that at that moment I remember dancing and just thinking, like wow, we pulled it off...like we threw this epic wedding and we are so happy. &amp;nbsp;I don&#039;t know if anything in life can top this happiness and if nothing else does I am ok with that because it was epic.\n\n\n&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;\n\n&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I don&#039;t necessarily have post wedding blues - but I do feel a few regrets of things that I didn&#039;t get to do. &amp;nbsp;I can&#039;t seem to let them go. &amp;nbsp;My sister gave me a really pretty silver bracelet and I don&#039;t know why, but I didn&#039;t wear it the day of the wedding. &amp;nbsp;I felt so bad. &amp;nbsp;I know she wanted to gift me something to wear and I ended up wearing a bracelet that was significantly daintier and I just didn&#039;t want something too chunky. &amp;nbsp;I have been seriously thinking of asking the photographer to Photoshop the bracelet in ...is this crazy?? &amp;nbsp;probably. &amp;nbsp;I just feel like i should have worn it. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Another regret is that we didn&#039;t take shots with each bridal party member. &amp;nbsp;like individual shots. &amp;nbsp;It was like 40c and I think we were all just hoping to get out of the heat but now looking back I feel really bad that we don&#039;t have individual shots with each person in our wedding party.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m actually really annoyed about it the more I think about it. &amp;nbsp;I wish we had done different shots with the bridal party- maybe i&#039;ll feel different or better once i see the pictures. &amp;nbsp;I don&#039;t know. &amp;nbsp;ahh&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We did have group shots, and here is a sneak peek but not individuals :(&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Our photographer was great and started shooting Thursday night at our bachelor\/bachelorette party and took a few candids friday night and then sat and Sunday and joined us on our trip to tulum. &amp;nbsp;In total he said he has about 5000 pictures...I don&#039;t know if in the grand scheme of things it&#039;s a big deal not to have individual shots but for some reason I\"m really bothered by it. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The day we arrived there was a huge tropical storm and the wedding that took place that day had to totally move her outdoor wedding indoors and was very upset by this..i&#039;m sure she is full of regrets so I know that I should be grateful for the beautiful day we had and move forward but I just wondered if anyone else had any similar feelings after their wedding.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m sharing a few more shots. &amp;nbsp;We ended up doing our own flowers and I saved soooo much money. &amp;nbsp;I made our centre pieces and bouquets the night before. &amp;nbsp;My bouquet and the gazebo flowers were included in our package so I didn&#039;t make those but the other ones were done by myself.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I spent $250 canadian in flowers versus $1000 usd. &amp;nbsp;score!!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Any advice would be welcomed! I\"m just trying to shake off these few things that I feel bad about.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1899554,"PostDate":1435675350,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>We are just coming down from our post wedding high! \u00a0There is nothing quite like it. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I have been writing our wedding review but I wanted to write this post first to seek some advice from other past brides.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Everything went well, there were some small glitches that I will write more about on our review, but essentially the experience was the best time of my life. \u00a0It was a combination of the people who went, the beauty of the beach and resort that contributed to a perfect day. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>When we left the resort I started crying because I knew that I had just spent the best time of my life at this resort with a group of people that I may never have all together again. \u00a0Our guests traveled from England, Peru, Spain, parts of Mexico,Toronto and Windsor so it's probably safe to say that they won't all be in the same room again. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I have never felt an overwhelming feeling of happiness and gratitude as this before and the advice I took with me from previous brides was to stop and really take it in. \u00a0There was a point where I was doing the bouquet toss and my dad's wife introduce a Mexican tradition which is to do a serpent dance (follow the leader type of dance) and all the women were wearing veils that she had made and they were dancing around me...everyone was so in the moment and so happy that at that moment I remember dancing and just thinking, like wow, we pulled it off...like we threw this epic wedding and we are so happy. \u00a0I don't know if anything in life can top this happiness and if nothing else does I am ok with that because it was epic.<br><br>\n\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1899554]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-49481300-1435689535.jpg\" title=\"IMG_4498.JPG - Size: 114.34KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-49481300-1435689535.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"IMG_4498.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1899554]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-00308100-1435689563.jpg\" title=\"IMG_4497.JPG - Size: 108.91KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-00308100-1435689563.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"IMG_4497.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<br>\n\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I don't necessarily have post wedding blues - but I do feel a few regrets of things that I didn't get to do. \u00a0I can't seem to let them go. \u00a0My sister gave me a really pretty silver bracelet and I don't know why, but I didn't wear it the day of the wedding. \u00a0I felt so bad. \u00a0I know she wanted to gift me something to wear and I ended up wearing a bracelet that was significantly daintier and I just didn't want something too chunky. \u00a0I have been seriously thinking of asking the photographer to Photoshop the bracelet in ...is this crazy?? \u00a0probably. \u00a0I just feel like i should have worn it. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Another regret is that we didn't take shots with each bridal party member. \u00a0like individual shots. \u00a0It was like 40c and I think we were all just hoping to get out of the heat but now looking back I feel really bad that we don't have individual shots with each person in our wedding party.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm actually really annoyed about it the more I think about it. \u00a0I wish we had done different shots with the bridal party- maybe i'll feel different or better once i see the pictures. \u00a0I don't know. \u00a0ahh\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We did have group shots, and here is a sneak peek but not individuals <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/><\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1899554]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-54647100-1435689579.jpg\" title=\"IMG_4495.JPG - Size: 204.49KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-54647100-1435689579.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"IMG_4495.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1899554]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-23009500-1435689592.jpg\" title=\"IMG_4496.JPG - Size: 138.47KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-23009500-1435689592.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"IMG_4496.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our photographer was great and started shooting Thursday night at our bachelor\/bachelorette party and took a few candids friday night and then sat and Sunday and joined us on our trip to tulum. \u00a0In total he said he has about 5000 pictures...I don't know if in the grand scheme of things it's a big deal not to have individual shots but for some reason I\"m really bothered by it. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The day we arrived there was a huge tropical storm and the wedding that took place that day had to totally move her outdoor wedding indoors and was very upset by this..i'm sure she is full of regrets so I know that I should be grateful for the beautiful day we had and move forward but I just wondered if anyone else had any similar feelings after their wedding.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm sharing a few more shots. \u00a0We ended up doing our own flowers and I saved soooo much money. \u00a0I made our centre pieces and bouquets the night before. \u00a0My bouquet and the gazebo flowers were included in our package so I didn't make those but the other ones were done by myself.<\/p>\n<p>I spent $250 canadian in flowers versus $1000 usd. \u00a0score!!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1899554]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-76552600-1435688262.jpg\" title=\"Wedding 522.JPG - Size: 192.31KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-76552600-1435688262.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"Wedding 522.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1899554]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-94478400-1435688472.jpg\" title=\"Wedding 528.JPG - Size: 121.04KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-94478400-1435688472.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"Wedding 528.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1899554]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-11540500-1435689689.jpg\" title=\"Wedding 529.JPG - Size: 130.28KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-11540500-1435689689.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"Wedding 529.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1899554]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-68495500-1435689739.jpg\" title=\"Wedding 537.JPG - Size: 114.21KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_06_2015\/post-277519-0-68495500-1435689739.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"Wedding 537.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Any advice would be welcomed! I\"m just trying to shake off these few things that I feel bad about.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Married on June 20th, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess Riviera Gazebo & Reception at the Chill Out with 60 guests<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>My review thread: \u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79344-grand-sunset-princess-platinum-yucatan-princess-wedding\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79344-grand-sunset-princess-platinum-yucatan-princess-wedding\/<\/a>","Email":"rebecca.valero@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1396968452,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1439827749","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":132,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"veryvalentine","Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"174.90.222.46","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"<strong>Edited by calgarybride2015, 30 June 2015 - 03:27 PM.<\/strong>","EditDate":1435678037,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":6,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"ebfd805b16c8b8d72b99f4fc13406b9b","RawContent":"All your photos are gorgeous. I think all us past DW brides can attest the sadness you feel that you may never relive that week again with all your close friends and family.   But you have memories and stories and it will be all everyone talks about for months to come!!! Some of us are planning a 1 year trip together. \n\n\nWe all have regrets but you need to move past them. You can&#039;t change them. I regret not spending more time with everyone. \n\n\nWith respect to the bracelet I wouldn&#039;t have it photoshopped in. But that&#039;s me. If it&#039;s bothering you I&#039;d sit down with your sister and tell her how you are feeling.  I&#039;m sure she is more than ok and the convo will make you both feel better. \n\n\nWe didn&#039;t do group shots with each person of the bridal party individually either. Just men and women then all together. I&#039;m ok with it because we have candid ones of us with most people from the week and the wedding day.  \n\n\nCan&#039;t wait to see more. \n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1899557,"PostDate":1435677492,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                All your photos are gorgeous. I think all us past DW brides can attest the sadness you feel that you may never relive that week again with all your close friends and family.   But you have memories and stories and it will be all everyone talks about for months to come!!! Some of us are planning a 1 year trip together. <br><br>\nWe all have regrets but you need to move past them. You can't change them. I regret not spending more time with everyone. <br><br>\nWith respect to the bracelet I wouldn't have it photoshopped in. But that's me. If it's bothering you I'd sit down with your sister and tell her how you are feeling.  I'm sure she is more than ok and the convo will make you both feel better. <br><br>\nWe didn't do group shots with each person of the bridal party individually either. Just men and women then all together. I'm ok with it because we have candid ones of us with most people from the week and the wedding day.  <br><br>\nCan't wait to see more. <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"64.53.250.35","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4aa3d10cf546c65649ad779fa0beadf7","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;My hubby (!) and I stayed four extra days after our guests left (they all stayed 7 days), and we thought we would be so ready to have time to ourselves by the end of the week, but I cried like a baby when we were in the lobby seeing everyone off to the airport. I just wanted everyone to stay with us! There is something so incredibly special about having so many different people from different places and different parts of your life all together, and it is sad when you think that it won&#039;t likely ever happen again. I definitely feel your pain on that part!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1899558,"PostDate":1435677949,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>My hubby (!) and I stayed four extra days after our guests left (they all stayed 7 days), and we thought we would be so ready to have time to ourselves by the end of the week, but I cried like a baby when we were in the lobby seeing everyone off to the airport. I just wanted everyone to stay with us! There is something so incredibly special about having so many different people from different places and different parts of your life all together, and it is sad when you think that it won't likely ever happen again. I definitely feel your pain on that part!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rachelia160@aim.com","IpAddress":"66.61.104.237","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1388717497,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275855.jpg?_r=1435853657","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"rachelia160","Id":275855,"Name":"rachelia160","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7a59b8921184f131262fd5b4df6cf7ad","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Everything looks beautiful from what I can see in the photos. Where did you grab your flowers from? I was thinking of adding babies breath to my centerpieces, but didn&#039;t know where I could grab some in Mexico. I&#039;m really excited to hear\/see more about the wedding and your photographer pictures. I&#039;m sure once you see those you will be much happier! :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Ps. Are you by any chance selling those lovely gold vases? haha&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1899559,"PostDate":1435678149,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Everything looks beautiful from what I can see in the photos. Where did you grab your flowers from? I was thinking of adding babies breath to my centerpieces, but didn't know where I could grab some in Mexico. I'm really excited to hear\/see more about the wedding and your photographer pictures. I'm sure once you see those you will be much happier! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>Ps. Are you by any chance selling those lovely gold vases? haha<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>\u00a0<br><br><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;1\/st\/20151215\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/ec4b\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><br><br><br><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1419423414,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1436293677","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.114.70.163","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"09f7d3c6b1b4e7ee773dcd32291273ee","RawContent":"I agree @[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] no photoshop- but I&#039;ve been worrying about it.  It was your advice that I was listening to over and over in my head when we taking in the good moments.  \n\n\n@[member=\"rachelia160\"] I agree!!! I know myself so well that I knew that I wouldn&#039;t want to be around once our guests left.  We decided to arrive 4 days before our guests to plan but we left with the group.  I had to say goodbye to my dad at the hotel as he was going back to his home in mexico so I was probably even more emotional because of that and everything heightened.  I was happy to leave with the group and share in that travel experience. \n\n\n@[member=\"perianjay\"] \n\nI have the business card of the flower store.  You have to order the baby&#039;s breath ahead of time but I think it was like 150 pesos for a huge bunch. \n\n\nThe vases my dad bought in veraCruz and we actually ended up gifting them to Katy from Love and Lace to add her to her decor repertoire.  I have her contact info if you need.  But I&#039;m sure she&#039;ll rent them out. She was so helpful... We sourced all our decorations and sparklers through her.  Im on the go train but I&#039;ll find the flower business card for you.  ;) \n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1899564,"PostDate":1435680528,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I agree @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> no photoshop- but I've been worrying about it.  It was your advice that I was listening to over and over in my head when we taking in the good moments.  <br><br>\n@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"275855\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/275855-rachelia160\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">rachelia160<\/span><\/a> I agree!!! I know myself so well that I knew that I wouldn't want to be around once our guests left.  We decided to arrive 4 days before our guests to plan but we left with the group.  I had to say goodbye to my dad at the hotel as he was going back to his home in mexico so I was probably even more emotional because of that and everything heightened.  I was happy to leave with the group and share in that travel experience. <br><br>\n@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281478\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281478-perianjay\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">perianjay<\/span><\/a> <br>\nI have the business card of the flower store.  You have to order the baby's breath ahead of time but I think it was like 150 pesos for a huge bunch. <br><br>\nThe vases my dad bought in veraCruz and we actually ended up gifting them to Katy from Love and Lace to add her to her decor repertoire.  I have her contact info if you need.  But I'm sure she'll rent them out. She was so helpful... We sourced all our decorations and sparklers through her.  Im on the go train but I'll find the flower business card for you.  <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/> <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Married on June 20th, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess Riviera Gazebo & Reception at the Chill Out with 60 guests<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>My review thread: \u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79344-grand-sunset-princess-platinum-yucatan-princess-wedding\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79344-grand-sunset-princess-platinum-yucatan-princess-wedding\/<\/a>","Email":"rebecca.valero@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1396968452,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1439827749","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":132,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"veryvalentine","Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"64.147.11.58","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":5,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7cd2a5bf147eb854f813a9aa861dfe51","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;I LOVE your post, because I totally have \"regrets\" too. &amp;nbsp;I hate to even call them regrets. &amp;nbsp;For example I was getting mad at my husband the other night because we never took photos on the pier (because he was over it and it was hot and we were both hungry and thirsty). &amp;nbsp;I should have pushed him to take them, but I &amp;nbsp;didn&#039;t so now I really wish I had those pictures.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Oh and I also started crying the week we got back at work, saying I wish we stayed longer and had more time alone. &amp;nbsp;Unfortunately we only ended up having 2 1\/2 days alone and it was not enough! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;In hindsight I wouldn&#039;t have changed anything, but wish I could do it all again. &amp;nbsp;It was the most amazing time and if you or any of you other ladies on here are anything like me. &amp;nbsp;You planned a great wedding, everyone had the time of their life, you are married to the best partner for you everything else now seems blah! &amp;nbsp;So we find little things to pick apart because maybe it wasn&#039;t all that great and everyday life isn&#039;t that blah to planning the most amazing day(s) of our life. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Just my thoughts...I have been feeling this too and thinking about it a lot. &amp;nbsp;Oh and writing this totally made me tear up! &amp;nbsp;Because it really was an amazing time and I know that despite the little things we didn&#039;t do, it was still epic!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1899566,"PostDate":1435685493,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>I LOVE your post, because I totally have \"regrets\" too. \u00a0I hate to even call them regrets. \u00a0For example I was getting mad at my husband the other night because we never took photos on the pier (because he was over it and it was hot and we were both hungry and thirsty). \u00a0I should have pushed him to take them, but I \u00a0didn't so now I really wish I had those pictures.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Oh and I also started crying the week we got back at work, saying I wish we stayed longer and had more time alone. \u00a0Unfortunately we only ended up having 2 1\/2 days alone and it was not enough! \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>In hindsight I wouldn't have changed anything, but wish I could do it all again. \u00a0It was the most amazing time and if you or any of you other ladies on here are anything like me. \u00a0You planned a great wedding, everyone had the time of their life, you are married to the best partner for you everything else now seems blah! \u00a0So we find little things to pick apart because maybe it wasn't all that great and everyday life isn't that blah to planning the most amazing day(s) of our life. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Just my thoughts...I have been feeling this too and thinking about it a lot. \u00a0Oh and writing this totally made me tear up! \u00a0Because it really was an amazing time and I know that despite the little things we didn't do, it was still epic!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"sabrabenes@gmail.com","IpAddress":"64.147.11.58","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1403194476,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278603.jpg?_r=1405559586","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Sabes44","Id":278603,"Name":"Sabes44","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"96.48.159.21","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4e182ad115e6703a2350bb6e648c4faa","RawContent":"I love the idea of the serpent dance during the bouquet toss, it totally looks like so much fun! \n\n\nI&#039;m sorry you have regrets and I know that I can only imagine what you&#039;re feeling since I&#039;m still in the planning stage so I can on,y empathize with you but try to focus on all the positive things instead of the negative. From what I can tell, you and your guests had an awesome time! In the planning stages, and this is a personal fear of mine, I&#039;m afraid that my guests will not have fun and wonder why they paid so much money to go to a boring wedding! I am hoping that my guests have the best time of our lives and they remember our wedding as one they had a great time going to. Well it seems you successfully pulled this off and you shouldn&#039;t regret this at all. You brought family from so many different parts of the world and you should be so happy that your wedding brought them all together for such a joyful occasion. This reunion may not happen again but you made it possible to even happen once in everyone&#039;s life.","Attachments":[],"Id":1899578,"PostDate":1435705016,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I love the idea of the serpent dance during the bouquet toss, it totally looks like so much fun! <br><br>\nI'm sorry you have regrets and I know that I can only imagine what you're feeling since I'm still in the planning stage so I can on,y empathize with you but try to focus on all the positive things instead of the negative. From what I can tell, you and your guests had an awesome time! In the planning stages, and this is a personal fear of mine, I'm afraid that my guests will not have fun and wonder why they paid so much money to go to a boring wedding! I am hoping that my guests have the best time of our lives and they remember our wedding as one they had a great time going to. Well it seems you successfully pulled this off and you shouldn't regret this at all. You brought family from so many different parts of the world and you should be so happy that your wedding brought them all together for such a joyful occasion. This reunion may not happen again but you made it possible to even happen once in everyone's life. \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"My planning thread: <a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79425-wafflesmom-moon-palace-planning-thread-january-23-2016\/\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79425-wafflesmom-moon-palace-planning-thread-january-23-2016\/<\/a><br><br>\n<p><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;4;484\/st\/20160123\/e\/Our+Wedding\/dt\/-2\/k\/44c5\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>","Email":"jerilee.valenzuela@shaw.ca","IpAddress":"24.114.26.77","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1410084185,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279721.jpg?_r=1441055220","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Wafflesmom","Id":279721,"Name":"Wafflesmom","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"216.84.102.233","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"272bb5682b97e5cea196ebacf873da01","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"veryvalentine\"] congratulations!!! and i can totally relate. i hate that we dont have any individual shots either. :\/ it really bothers me, but im trying to focus on the good pictures we DO have.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1899598,"PostDate":1435743120,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277519\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277519-veryvalentine\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">veryvalentine<\/span><\/a> congratulations!!! and i can totally relate. i hate that we dont have any individual shots either. :\/ it really bothers me, but im trying to focus on the good pictures we DO have.\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>58 guests plus bride and groom<br>\nCeremony: Gazebo<br>\nReception: Pool Deck","Email":"smileitseb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"50.90.104.129","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1394209469,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277044.jpg?_r=1432531828","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":241,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"smileitseb","Id":277044,"Name":"smileitseb","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"199.126.252.6","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"678796a1e417d4ba083548a2d1af36da","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Congratulations! Everything looked so good and I&#039;m happy that you consider this the best time ever :). I think we always have some kind of regret, but I wouldn&#039;t let that hold you back from enjoying your memories at its fullest. You know for a lot of us this is our first wedding, and as usual with first times, there&#039;s always things we learn in the process and things we wouldn&#039;t do again if we had to, so I think some regrets are normal. I really would try to get past them and maybe if talking to your sister helps I would do that :).&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1899616,"PostDate":1435750388,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Congratulations! Everything looked so good and I'm happy that you consider this the best time ever <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>. I think we always have some kind of regret, but I wouldn't let that hold you back from enjoying your memories at its fullest. You know for a lot of us this is our first wedding, and as usual with first times, there's always things we learn in the process and things we wouldn't do again if we had to, so I think some regrets are normal. I really would try to get past them and maybe if talking to your sister helps I would do that <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>.\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359748704,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.85.127.174","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79333,"EditedBy":"<strong>Edited by vancouverpetunia, 01 July 2015 - 12:52 PM.<\/strong>","EditDate":1435755132,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5937ce773a7a68d399d8fd9d34aa5437","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:14px;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Thank you for your post. Since I&#039;m planning my wedding for 9 months from now, I haven&#039;t even thought of the emotions as it all ends. Good to be prepared, although I suspect you never know how you&#039;ll feel, until is all happens! It seems like you have so few regrets among a multitude of happy memories.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;It&#039;s never going to be perfect, and you even said you had the best time of your life.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;I know this is probably lame advice and you are already trying to do this, but just hold onto the good stuff and let those regrets go. I like what @[member=\"Sabes44\"] said: \"&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;In hindsight I wouldn&#039;t have changed anything, but wish I could do it all again.\" &amp;nbsp;If you couldn&#039;t change anything but had the opportunity to do it all over again, would you? I bet you would!&amp;nbsp; :)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"Wafflesmom\"] I know how you feel about wanting to make sure guests have a great time. I feel the same way. I take consolation in the fact that I went to a DW a number of years ago (where I met my FI!) and I think everyone, us included, had an amazing time. People still talk about it. And for us, it&#039;s not even that it was great because we met there - we didn&#039;t see each other again for a year. So it&#039;s not like our memories are tinged with romance. :wub:  However, the downside to that is we had such a fantastic time I&#039;m worried our own DW won&#039;t live up to my expectations!&amp;nbsp; :P&lt;\/p&gt;\n\n&lt;p&gt;P.S.&amp;nbsp;@[member=\"veryvalentine\"] How did you get your flowers into the resort? Did you have to pay any vendor fees? I want very simple centrepieces, very similar to yours, so we could probably do them ourselves, but I don&#039;t know how that would work. Can you send the contact info for the florist, too?&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1899627,"PostDate":1435755089,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><span  style=\"font-size:14px\"><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Thank you for your post. Since I'm planning my wedding for 9 months from now, I haven't even thought of the emotions as it all ends. Good to be prepared, although I suspect you never know how you'll feel, until is all happens! It seems like you have so few regrets among a multitude of happy memories.<\/span><\/span><span  style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">It's never going to be perfect, and you even said you had the best time of your life.<\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">I know this is probably lame advice and you are already trying to do this, but just hold onto the good stuff and let those regrets go. I like what @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"278603\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/278603-sabes44\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Sabes44<\/span><\/a> said: \"<\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">In hindsight I wouldn't have changed anything, but wish I could do it all again.\" \u00a0If you couldn't change anything but had the opportunity to do it all over again, would you? I bet you would!\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"279721\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/279721-wafflesmom\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Wafflesmom<\/span><\/a> I know how you feel about wanting to make sure guests have a great time. I feel the same way. I take consolation in the fact that I went to a DW a number of years ago (where I met my FI!) and I think everyone, us included, had an amazing time. People still talk about it. And for us, it's not even that it was great because we met there - we didn't see each other again for a year. So it's not like our memories are tinged with romance. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wub.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':wub:' \/>\u00a0\u00a0However, the downside to that is we had such a fantastic time I'm worried our own DW won't live up to my expectations!\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/tongue.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':P' \/><\/p>\n<br><p>P.S.\u00a0@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277519\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277519-veryvalentine\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">veryvalentine<\/span><\/a> How did you get your flowers into the resort? Did you have to pay any vendor fees? I want very simple centrepieces, very similar to yours, so we could probably do them ourselves, but I don't know how that would work. Can you send the contact info for the florist, too?<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>- Erin<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?p=1893268'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?p=1893268<\/a>","Email":"ekjzwedding@gmail.com","IpAddress":"24.85.127.174","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1417435045,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"vancouverpetunia","Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","IsOnline":false}}],"Id":"79333","Title":"After The Wedding!","LastPostDate":1442420146},"Pages":{"TotalItems":22,"TotalPages":3,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":10,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":20},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
