> Time: 1443195911 / Fri, 25 Sep 2015 15:45:11 +0000
> URL: /index.php?/REST/users/messenger/addReply?SessionId=4900d83b2df2f100b1cc36a3621f7303
> User kuoling (282701)
array (
  '/REST/users/messenger/addReply?SessionId' => '4900d83b2df2f100b1cc36a3621f7303',
  'module' => 'REST',
  'section' => 'run',
  'request_method' => 'post',
  'app' => 'REST_Service',
  'application' => 'users',
  'class' => 'messenger',
  'operation' => 'addReply',
  'SessionId' => '4900d83b2df2f100b1cc36a3621f7303',
  'conversationId' => '11521',
  'messageContent' => 'Looks like you are right on track! 

Ultimate package only covers one hour of photography. My fiance\'s coworker actually got married at secrets the vine as well and they used resort\'s adventure photography and they liked it.  I asked Yamina for other options (w/o a fee) and she gave me Juan Navarro. Juan looks decent and has better rate than advature so that\'s what I\'m going for.  You should ask Yamina again see if there are other options.  You probably already know, there are many good local photographers in Cancun such as del sol and fineArt. Outside vendor fee isn\'t that high compared to other resorts so if you really like a particular photographer you should still go for it.

I actually haven\'t thought about the make up...I guess I\'ll let the resort do it? If you are worried you can have a trial? Are you paying for all your bridesmaids makeup/hair?

What theme are you having? Do you plan to add many additional decor to your ceremony and reception?',
  'sessionId' => '4900d83b2df2f100b1cc36a3621f7303',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
